the father of a young child killed in a  high-speed crash has now also been  arrested thank you for joining us  tonight at six  i'm kirsten joyce both parents of the  child now face charges for this crash  twenty-three-year-old lauren prescha is  accused of driving impaired  when she crashed into a marquee sign  killing her 22 month old son  the crash happened sunday at the  intersection of lake mead and rampart  metro police now say the father 23 year  old cameron hubbard jones is  also responsible christian drummond  joins us live from  the newsroom with the latest  developments in the investigation  kristen  kyrsten police are charging hubbard  jones with reckless driving  officers say he was also going more than  100 miles per hour on rampart boulevard  before the deadly crash  this is dash camera video showing two  cars speeding  hubbard jones was in a mercedes and  prussia in a hyundai according to police  officers claimed the parents were likely  racing each other on the street  police report prussia driving 121 miles  per hour in a 45 mile per hour zone  before hitting a car and then slamming  into a marquis signed support  with her son in the back seat a retired  metro sergeant watched the video today  he says a quick flash possibly shows the  moment of the deadly crash and says  the father is just as responsible as the  mother  why was he going fast there's no need  just because they're going going home he  doesn't need  he should have probably got on the on  the phone and said my wife girlfriend  what  whatever their relationship is has got  my child in the car and she is driving  you know extremely fast on this roadway  a police report says hubbard jones  claimed the two were in the process of a  custody exchange  meanwhile lauren prussia was in court  again this morning  her lawyer withdrew from the case and  another public defender is being  assigned  presche is being held on a 50-thousand  dollar bail and is due back in court  tomorrow  now a memorial at the crash site  continues to grow with balloons toys and  candles  many who don't know the child or family  tell me they've continued to come  out here or out there to pay their  respects a candlelight vigil for him is  scheduled for tomorrow night at 8  o'clock  at buckskin baskin park reporting live  in the newsroom kristen drummond 8 news  now
 

